  "Question": "If \\(a\\) represents the side length of a square (unit: cm), what does the algebraic expression \\(4a\\) represent for this square?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Area",
    "B": "Perimeter",
    "C": "Diagonal length",
    "D": "Half the side length"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A square has 4 sides, each of length \\(a\\). The sum of the side lengths, \\(4a\\), is its perimeter. Its area should be \\(a^2\\).",
